(ned ROTARY PROBE -- find the B axis centreline and set G55. Two stations.)
(Operator 2026-08-12. Start ABOVE the bar, roughly over it, about 10 mm up.)

(THE APPROX BAR DIAMETER IS A MOTION BOUND, NOT A MEASUREMENT. Operator:)
(write in approx bar diameter, 1.25in, but it should not appear in any)
(calculations. It only decides how far to step aside to clear the bar and how)
(far to cross to the far side. It is never in the arithmetic that produces X0)
(or Z0, so a wrong guess costs travel and nothing else. The real diameter is)
(DERIVED below and reported.)

(WHY THE FLANKS COME BEFORE THE CROWN. The crown is only the crown at the)
(centre, and the centre is the unknown. Probing down first would measure some)
(point on the cylinder and call it the top. So: two flanks give the centre,)
(then the crown is probed AT that centre, where it is genuinely the highest)
(point and no radius correction applies.)

(THE PROBE RADIUS CANCELS IN X: the left touch stops with the flank at)
(xl + R, the right at xr - R, so the mean is the axis for any probe. It does)
(NOT cancel in the half-width, which is why the probe diameter is a real)
(parameter: h = [[xr - xl] - D] / 2.)

(THE GEOMETRY. With half-width h at depth d below the crown,)
(  r^2 = h^2 + [r - d]^2   ->   r = [h^2 + d^2] / [2d])
(so the radius, and hence the bar diameter, falls out of the measurement.)

(DATUM IS G55. Operator: g54 is my fuck around system. Nothing here writes)
(G54 - every offset goes to G10 L2 P2.)
o<rotary_probe> sub
  (ONLY THE FIRST THREE ARE ON SCREEN. The rest are travel limits and feeds:)
  (they have no bearing on the answer, and a box the operator never changes is)
  (a box that eventually gets changed by accident. Every one still carries a)
  (default here, because SubCallButton refuses to call at all if an argument)
  (has neither a widget nor one.)
  #<rp_pdia>   = #1 (=9.1281 probe diameter mm - the one number the maths uses)
  #<rp_approx> = #2 (=31.75 approx bar diameter - initial move only)
  #<rp_gap>    = #3 (=304.8 Y to the second station mm - 12 in)
  #<rp_maxx>   = #4 (=40.0 max X search)
  #<rp_maxz>   = #5 (=40.0 max Z search)
  #<rp_ffast>  = #6 (=100.0 find feed)
  #<rp_fslow>  = #7 (=10.0 latch feed)
  #<rp_ftrav>  = #8 (=1000.0 traverse feed)
  #<pdia>  = #<rp_pdia>
  #<approx> = #<rp_approx>
  #<gap>   = #<rp_gap>
  #<maxx>  = #<rp_maxx>
  #<maxz>  = #<rp_maxz>
  #<ffast> = #<rp_ffast>
  #<fslow> = #<rp_fslow>
  #<ftrav> = #<rp_ftrav>
  o1 if [#<pdia> LE 0]
    (abort, ROTARY PROBE: probe diameter is required - it is the one number the maths needs)
  o1 endif
  o2 if [#<approx> LE 0]
    #<approx> = 31.75
  o2 endif
  o4 if [#<gap> EQ 0]
    #<gap> = 304.8
  o4 endif
  o5 if [#<maxx> LE 0]
    #<maxx> = 40.0
  o5 endif
  o6 if [#<maxz> LE 0]
    #<maxz> = 40.0
  o6 endif
  o7 if [#<ffast> LE 0]
    #<ffast> = 100.0
  o7 endif
  o8 if [#<fslow> LE 0]
    #<fslow> = 10.0
  o8 endif
  o9 if [#<ftrav> LE 0]
    #<ftrav> = 1000.0
  o9 endif
  o10 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, ROTARY PROBE: switch to MM first)
  o10 endif
  (NO M66 PRE-CHECK. M66 reads motion.digital-in-N, and the probe is not on)
  (one: digital-in-02 is SHAFT STOPPED here - ned5_iron.hal:530.)
  (The old guard therefore fired whenever the spindle was stopped, which is)
  (always, and the cycle could never start. G38.2 refuses on its own if the)
  (probe is tripped when it begins, so nothing is lost by dropping it.)

  (the park height is wherever the operator left it: they lowered to suit)
  (whatever probe is in the spindle, and that is the only safe crossover Z)
  #<zpark> = #5422
  (THE ONLY PLACE approx IS ALLOWED. Operator 2026-08-12: "don't use that)
  (number for anything besides the initial move ... move it by D/2 + probe D".)
  (Nothing downstream reads it - X0, h, r and Z0 are all measured.)
  (DROP IS DERIVED FROM THE PARK, not typed. Operator 2026-08-12: parked)
  (about 5 mm above the bar, and the drop is bar/2 + 10 from there -- which)
  (puts the probe roughly 5 mm below the centreline, comfortably onto the)
  (flank. Still only the approximate diameter, still only a move.)
  (+20, not +10: another 10 mm of plunge. Operator 2026-08-12 - "just in case)
  (it doesn't measure D correctly". Deeper flanks give a bigger half-width h,)
  (and r = [h^2 + d^2] / 2d is better conditioned the further h and d get from)
  (zero, so the derived diameter tightens up.)
  #<drop>  = [[#<approx> / 2.0] + 20.0]
  #<step>  = [[#<approx> / 2.0] + #<pdia>]
  #<cross> = [#<approx> + [#<pdia> * 2.0]]
  #<st>    = 1
  o20 while [#<st> LE 2]
    #<y0> = #5421
    (--- 1. aside and down, clear of the bar --------------------------------)
    G90
    G1 X[#5420 - #<step>] F[#<ftrav>]
    #<zp> = [#<zpark> - #<drop>]
    G1 Z[#<zp>] F[#<ftrav>]
    (--- 2. near flank ------------------------------------------------------)
    G38.2 X[#5420 + #<maxx>] F[#<ffast>]
    o30 if [#5070 EQ 0]
      G1 Z[#<zpark>] F[#<ftrav>]
      (abort, ROTARY PROBE: near flank never touched - is the drop deep enough to be beside the bar?)
    o30 endif
    #<xf> = #5061
    G1 X[#<xf> - 2.0] F[#<ftrav>]
    G38.2 X[#<xf> + 4.0] F[#<fslow>]
    o31 if [#5070 EQ 0]
      G1 Z[#<zpark>] F[#<ftrav>]
      (abort, ROTARY PROBE: near flank slow latch found nothing)
    o31 endif
    #<xl> = #5061
    (--- 3. cross ABOVE the bar, never through it ---------------------------)
    G1 X[#<xl> - 2.0] F[#<ftrav>]
    G1 Z[#<zpark>] F[#<ftrav>]
    G1 X[#<xl> + #<cross>] F[#<ftrav>]
    G1 Z[#<zp>] F[#<ftrav>]
    (--- 4. far flank -------------------------------------------------------)
    G38.2 X[#5420 - #<maxx>] F[#<ffast>]
    o32 if [#5070 EQ 0]
      G1 Z[#<zpark>] F[#<ftrav>]
      (abort, ROTARY PROBE: far flank never touched - increase the approx bar diameter)
    o32 endif
    #<xg> = #5061
    G1 X[#<xg> + 2.0] F[#<ftrav>]
    G38.2 X[#<xg> - 4.0] F[#<fslow>]
    o33 if [#5070 EQ 0]
      G1 Z[#<zpark>] F[#<ftrav>]
      (abort, ROTARY PROBE: far flank slow latch found nothing)
    o33 endif
    #<xr> = #5061
    (--- 5. centre in X, then the crown AT that centre ----------------------)
    #<x0> = [[#<xl> + #<xr>] / 2.0]
    #<h>  = [[[#<xr> - #<xl>] - #<pdia>] / 2.0]
    o34 if [#<h> LE 0]
      G1 Z[#<zpark>] F[#<ftrav>]
      (abort, ROTARY PROBE: flanks came out narrower than the probe - bad touch)
    o34 endif
    G1 X[#<xr> + 2.0] F[#<ftrav>]
    G1 Z[#<zpark>] F[#<ftrav>]
    G1 X[#<x0>] F[#<ftrav>]
    G38.2 Z[#5422 - #<maxz>] F[#<ffast>]
    o35 if [#5070 EQ 0]
      G1 Z[#<zpark>] F[#<ftrav>]
      (abort, ROTARY PROBE: crown never touched)
    o35 endif
    #<zc1> = #5063
    G1 Z[#<zc1> + 2.0] F[#<ftrav>]
    G38.2 Z[#<zc1> - 4.0] F[#<fslow>]
    o36 if [#5070 EQ 0]
      G1 Z[#<zpark>] F[#<ftrav>]
      (abort, ROTARY PROBE: crown slow latch found nothing)
    o36 endif
    #<zc> = #5063
    G1 Z[#<zpark>] F[#<ftrav>]
    (--- 6. the answer ------------------------------------------------------)
    #<d>  = [#<zc> - #<zp>]
    o37 if [#<d> LE 0.001]
      (abort, ROTARY PROBE: flanks were not below the crown - increase the drop)
    o37 endif
    #<r>  = [[[#<h> * #<h>] + [#<d> * #<d>]] / [2.0 * #<d>]]
    #<z0> = [#<zc> - #<r>]
    (r IS THE RADIUS. It was labelled dia and it is not - the bar came out)
    (32.71 across when it read 16.36, which is exactly a factor of two and)
    (exactly the sort of thing that gets believed.)
    (RESULTS GO INTO PARAMETERS so the page can show them: the log is not)
    (where the operator is looking.)
    o41 if [#<st> EQ 1]
      #3090 = #<x0>
      #3091 = #<z0>
      #3096 = [#<r> * 2.0]
    o41 else
      #3092 = #<x0>
      #3093 = #<z0>
      #3097 = [#<r> * 2.0]
    o41 endif
    (PRINT, ROTARY station #<st>: X0 #<x0> Z0 #<z0> crown #<zc> h #<h> d #<d> radius #<r>)
    o40 if [#<st> EQ 1]
      #<x1> = #<x0>
      #<za> = #<z0>
      #<ya> = #<y0>
      (RAPID between stations. 12 in of empty air at the park height -- the)
      (height the operator themselves stopped at, so it is known clear -- and)
      (nothing is being measured on the way. Feeding it was just waiting.)
      G0 Y[#<y0> + #<gap>]
    o40 else
      #<x2> = #<x0>
      #<zb> = #<z0>
    o40 endif
    #<st> = [#<st> + 1]
  o20 endwhile

  (--- 7. alignment, and the datum from station 1 ---------------------------)
  #<dx> = [#<x2> - #<x1>]
  #<dz> = [#<zb> - #<za>]
  #3094 = #<dx>
  #3095 = #<dz>
  #3098 = #<gap>
  (PRINT, ROTARY ALIGNMENT over #<gap> mm: yaw dX #<dx> mm, droop dZ #<dz> mm)
  (PRINT, ROTARY: rotate B 180 and re-run - real misalignment keeps its sign, a bent bar flips it.)
  G1 Z[#<zpark>] F[#<ftrav>]
  G1 Y[#<ya>] F[#<ftrav>]
  G1 X[#<x1>] F[#<ftrav>]
  (G55 ONLY. G54 is the operator's scratch system and is never written here.)
  (DEAD CENTRE OF STATION 1, in all three. G10 L20 makes the CURRENT position)
  (read the value given -- and at this instant the spindle is back at the PARK)
  (height, not on the centreline. X and Y are genuinely at the station 1)
  (centre so they take 0 outright, but Z must be handed the distance from the)
  (axis up to where the tool actually is. Writing Z0 here would have put the)
  (datum a whole park-drop above the bar, and every depth after it would have)
  (been wrong by that much with nothing to show for it.)
  G10 L20 P2 X0 Y0 Z[#<zpark> - #<za>]
  (TEACH THE PARK POINT FROM THE MEASUREMENT. Operator 2026-08-12: the start)
  (position should become the centre this cycle just found -- station 1 is at)
  (the fixed head, so it is the best teach point there is, and each run makes)
  (the next one land closer.)
  (READ IT OFF THE OFFSET, NOT BY CONVERTING. The line above just made this)
  (very position read X0 Y0 in G55, so the G55 offsets ARE the machine)
  (coordinates of the centre -- #5241/#5242. Computing machine = work + offset)
  (by hand is the frame mistake that had the shoulder plunging 157 mm past)
  (the Z limit; there is no reason to repeat it when the number is sitting)
  (right there.)
  (Z IS DELIBERATELY NOT TAUGHT: the park height is a property of whatever)
  (probe is in the spindle, not of the bar, and it changes every time one is)
  (swapped. The operator owns that one.)
  (ALL THREE IN MACHINE COORDINATES. Operator 2026-08-12: repeatability then)
  (rests on HOMING, not on whatever work offset happened to be live -- and if)
  (precision is wanted, reprobe. #5241/2/3 are the G55 origin, and the line)
  (above just made this position read X0 Y0 in G55, so they ARE the machine)
  (coordinates of the centre.)
  (ONLY X AND Y ARE USED TO GO BACK. The bar diameter may differ next time,)
  (so the centre HEIGHT is not a property of the fixture -- Z is recorded for)
  (reference and for a sanity check, never to drive a move.)
  #3080 = #5241
  #3081 = #5242
  #3082 = #5243
  (PRINT, ROTARY: taught - bar centre X #3080 Y #3081 Z #3082 machine. GO TO BAR uses X and Y only.)
  (PRINT, ROTARY DONE: G55 X0 Z0 sits on the B centreline at station 1.)
o<rotary_probe> endsub
M2 (end program)
